  "html": "<div class=\"answer-row\"><div class=\"answer-paragraph\"><strong>Ablated‑version performance (win‑rate % against NaiveRAG)</strong></div><aside class=\"margin-citations\" aria-label=\"Citation margin notes\"></aside></div>\n<div class=\"answer-row\"><div class=\"answer-paragraph\"><div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Metric</th><th>Agriculture</th><th>CS</th><th>Legal</th><th>Mix</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>‑High</strong> (high‑level retrieval removed)</td><td>Comprehensiveness</td><td>34.8 % / 65.2 %</td><td>42.8 % / 57.2 %</td><td>23.6 % / 76.4 %</td><td>40.4 % / 59.6 %</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Diversity</td><td>27.2 % / 72.8 %</td><td>36.8 % / 63.2 %</td><td>16.8 % / 83.2 %</td><td>36.0 % / 64.0 %</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Empowerment</td><td>36.0 % / 64.0 %</td><td>42.4 % / 57.6 %</td><td>22.8 % / 77.2 %</td><td>47.6 % / 52.4 %</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Overall</td><td>35.2 % / 64.8 %</td><td>44.0 % / 56.0 %</td><td>22.0 % / 78.0 %</td><td>42.4 % / 57.6 %</td></tr><tr><td><strong>‑Low</strong> (low‑level retrieval removed)</td><td>Comprehensiveness</td><td>36.0 % / 64.0 %</td><td>43.2 % / 56.8 %</td><td>19.2 % / 80.8 %</td><td>36.0 % / 64.0 %</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Diversity</td><td>28.0 % / 72.0 %</td><td>39.6 % / 60.4 %</td><td>13.6 % / 86.4 %</td><td>33.2 % / 66.8 %</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Empowerment</td><td>34.8 % / 65.2 %</td><td>42.8 % / 57.2 %</td><td>16.4 % / 83.6 %</td><td>35.2 % / 64.8 %</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Overall</td><td>34.8 % / 65.2 %</td><td>43.6 % / 56.4 %</td><td>18.8 % / 81.2 %</td><td>35.2 % / 64.8 %</td></tr><tr><td><strong>‑Origin</strong> (original text removed)</td><td>Comprehensiveness</td><td>24.8 % / 75.2 %</td><td>39.2 % / 60.8 %</td><td>16.4 % / 83.6 %</td><td>44.4 % / 55.6 %</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Diversity</td><td>26.4 % / 73.6 %</td><td>44.8 % / 55.2 %</td><td>14.4 % / 85.6 %</td><td>25.6 % / 74.4 %</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Empowerment</td><td>32.0 % / 68.0 %</td><td>43.2 % / 56.8 %</td><td>17.2 % / 82.8 %</td><td>45.2 % / 54.8 %</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Overall</td><td>25.6 % / 74.4 %</td><td>39.2 % / 60.8 %</td><td>15.6 % / 84.4 %</td><td>44.4 % / 55.6 %</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><aside class=\"margin-citations\" aria-label=\"Citation margin notes\"></aside></div>\n<div class=\"answer-row\"><div class=\"answer-paragraph\">*Each cell shows “NaiveRAG win % / variant win %”. The numbers are taken directly from Table 2 of the paper, which compares each ablated version against the NaiveRAG baseline (not against the full LightRAG system)<button class=\"inline-citation\" aria-label=\"View C9, p.8, 4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)\">[C9]</button>.</div><aside class=\"margin-citations\" aria-label=\"Citation margin notes\"><button class=\"margin-citation\" aria-label=\"View C9, p.8, 4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)\"><span class=\"citation-location\">[C9] · p.8</span><span class=\"citation-section\">4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)</span></button></aside></div>\n<div class=\"answer-row\"><div class=\"answer-paragraph\"><strong>Interpretation (from the authors):</strong></div><aside class=\"margin-citations\" aria-label=\"Citation margin notes\"></aside></div>\n<ul>\n<li><div class=\"answer-row\"><div class=\"answer-paragraph\">The <strong>‑High</strong> variant removes high‑order retrieval, causing a notable drop in performance across most datasets and metrics<button class=\"inline-citation\" aria-label=\"View C10, p.8, 4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)\">[C10]</button>.</div><aside class=\"margin-citations\" aria-label=\"Citation margin notes\"><button class=\"margin-citation\" aria-label=\"View C10, p.8, 4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)\"><span class=\"citation-location\">[C10] · p.8</span><span class=\"citation-section\">4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)</span></button></aside></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"answer-row\"><div class=\"answer-paragraph\">The <strong>‑Low</strong> variant removes low‑level retrieval, which hurts depth of detail but retains good comprehensiveness<button class=\"inline-citation\" aria-label=\"View C10, p.8, 4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)\">[C10]</button>.</div><aside class=\"margin-citations\" aria-label=\"Citation margin notes\"><button class=\"margin-citation\" aria-label=\"View C10, p.8, 4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)\"><span class=\"citation-location\">[C10] · p.8</span><span class=\"citation-section\">4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)</span></button></aside></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"answer-row\"><div class=\"answer-paragraph\">The <strong>‑Origin</strong> variant eliminates the original text from retrieval; its performance remains comparable to the full system, sometimes even improving on certain datasets<button class=\"inline-citation\" aria-label=\"View C10, p.8, 4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)\">[C10]</button>.</div><aside class=\"margin-citations\" aria-label=\"Citation margin notes\"><button class=\"margin-citation\" aria-label=\"View C10, p.8, 4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)\"><span class=\"citation-location\">[C10] · p.8</span><span class=\"citation-section\">4.3 ABLATION STUDIES (RQ2)</span></button></aside></div></li>\n</ul>",
